# Hide on the Ceiling with two targets: if one is illegal as it resolves the other is still affected (CR 608.2b). Bot1 targets Bot2's Llanowar Elves and its
# own Ornithopter with X = 2; in response Bot2 Lightning Bolts its own Elves, which dies. The Ornithopter is exiled and returns at the beginning of the
# end step; the Elves, in the graveyard, is not an exiled card and does not.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Ornithopter
Hide on the Ceiling
Plains x2
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Ruby
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Forest x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hide on the Ceiling.Cast(X: 2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves; Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Exile = Ornithopter
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Ruby
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Lightning Bolt
